<section id="weaker">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading reveal">
            <span class="kicker">Honestly</span>
            <h2>Where fleet is weaker.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="rule-columns">
            <div class="rule-col reveal">
                <span class="rule-kicker">Two harnesses</span>
                <p>Agents run Claude Code, or Neovim with Claude beside it. Conductor, Claude Squad and others also run Codex, Gemini or OpenCode <a class="cmp-src" href="#src-S5b">S5b</a> <a class="cmp-src" href="#src-S6">S6</a>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rule-col reveal">
                <span class="rule-kicker">Terminal only</span>
                <p>No GUI and no visual diff review. Desktop apps such as Nimbalyst and Conductor offer one <a class="cmp-src" href="#src-S7">S7</a> <a class="cmp-src" href="#src-S5b">S5b</a>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rule-col reveal">
                <span class="rule-kicker">Windows first</span>
                <p>Windows is the main platform. Linux binaries are built and tested by CI but not yet used in anger; macOS builds from source only.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="install-note section-note reveal">On the roadmap, at high priority: embedding more harnesses and letting you use other editors. <a href="https://github.com/Redmern/fleet-tui/issues">Follow the roadmap on GitHub</a>.</p>
    </div>
</section>
